    "result_text": "The full suite is green (37 tests, 0 failures) and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule for owner creation in the Spring PetClinic REST app.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the sole `POST /api/owners` handler):\n- Added a check, alongside the existing telephone-uniqueness/household identity checks, that rejects a create with **409 Conflict** when the new owner's email (compared lower-cased) is already used by any existing owner.\n- Added a helper `isEmailAlreadyUsed(String email)` that streams `findAllOwners()` and matches on the lower-cased email. It follows the existing normalization idioms in this class (e.g. `normalizeName`, `findHouseholdMembers`). Email is optional, so a blank/missing email never collides.\n\nThe comparison is case-insensitive on both sides (the `Owner` entity already lower-cases email on store, but the helper lower-cases both sides defensively).\n\n**Test** \u2014 added `EmailUniqueTests` (acceptance-style, matching the existing `CpXX` black-box pattern) covering:\n- Duplicate email in a different case \u2192 409.\n- Two distinct emails \u2192 both accepted.\n\nAll 37 tests pass.",
